prompt_md:
A furniture maker's production-planning system has run for 20 years on servers in its factory data center. The vendor that wrote it no longer exists, so moving it would mean a long rewrite. The company wants a customer ordering website live within six weeks. The website must:

- read stock levels from the production-planning system;
- cost only for the capacity it uses;
- grow to handle the holiday rush.

Which deployment do you recommend?

A university's IT estate has exactly three parts:

- a student-records system on servers in the university's own data center;
- a course website in AWS that reads grades from the student-records system over a private network link;
- staff email from a SaaS provider.

Which statements are true? Select all that apply.
